In article <1991Jul24.135521.14532@bhpcpd.kembla.oz.au> dif@bhpcpd.kembla.oz.au (David Faulkner) writes:
|> What does the level rating of a spell mean (eg: invisibility (4)) ?
|> Does it reflect difficulty in transcribing, casting or both? How do you
|> relate that back to your own experience level.
|> 
|> Also, does using a spell have a recovery time similar to praying, or 
|> does it always come back "this spell is starting to be overused" etc.
|> after a couple of times? And, does re-reading a spellbook return you 
|> back to the beginning as far as spell usage is concerned?

The number in parenthesis next to the spell is the number of magic points
it takes to cast the spell.  Usually the more powerfull the spell the more
points it takes.  In my version of nethack the magic power is displayed
at the bottom of the screen.  When your magic power is lower than that
required to cast the spell, you have to wait until it recuperates (it comes
back like hit points).  However, when you forget the spell (spell is overused)
then you can't cast it again until you reread that particular spellbook.

